  "verbalization": "Botryorhodine C is associated with the target Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is a protein involved in epigenetic regulation. This enzyme is targeted by (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol, suggesting a complex regulatory pathway involving epigenetic modifications. Additionally, Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like is also targeted by (+)-1,5-Epoxy-nor-ketoguaia-11-ene, which directly interacts with prostate cells. The evidence suggests that Botryorhodine C may exert its effects through the modulation of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, potentially influencing cellular processes in prostate cells. The relationship is supported by multiple targets and their interaction with prostate cells, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
